1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,609
Last time the ruin could talk.

2
00:00:03,059 --> 00:00:05,233
Today it keeps a secret.

3
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:11,335
A crew that listens at the door gets one more answer further in.

4
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:17,437
That answer opens a side room, and a small story of its own.

5
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:27,887
And when they find what is in the room, the main screen stops being a window and becomes a film, for ten seconds.

6
00:00:29,087 --> 00:00:36,043
A clue is something the crew learns in one place that changes what happens in another.

7
00:00:36,493 --> 00:00:42,146
You already wrote one: Mark the Gallery put a place on the map.

8
00:00:42,596 --> 00:00:52,161
Today, two new words. learn, on an answer, writes a word down for this crew. learned, on another answer, counts the words.

9
00:00:52,611 --> 00:00:55,654
That is all it does: it counts.

10
00:00:56,104 --> 00:00:59,583
It cannot ask for a word by name.

11
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:03,511
There is one list for the whole ship.

12
00:01:03,961 --> 00:01:11,787
And the rule that shapes everything: the game reads the count when the crew opens the scene, once.

13
00:01:12,237 --> 00:01:18,759
If they open a call too early, going away and coming back does not help.

14
00:01:19,209 --> 00:01:23,557
So the clue has to come first on the road.

15
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:27,365
Every ship flies through the ring.

16
00:01:27,815 --> 00:01:30,424
So the first clue goes there.

17
00:01:30,874 --> 00:01:36,526
A place, on the same spot as the ring, with a role: plate.

18
00:01:36,976 --> 00:01:45,237
A beat, the same as last time: when a ship is within five hundred of the plate, Rook calls.

19
00:01:45,687 --> 00:01:46,991
And the scene.

20
00:01:47,441 --> 00:01:49,180
One take, two answers.

21
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,804
Here is the new part.

22
00:01:52,254 --> 00:01:56,602
Log the names, semicolon, learn names. names is my word.

23
00:01:57,052 --> 00:01:59,226
The crew never sees it.

24
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:01,850
They see Log the names.

25
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:04,354
Now the altar.

26
00:02:04,804 --> 00:02:08,717
One new answer, between the two that are there.

27
00:02:09,167 --> 00:02:16,559
Play the entry keyed to Dace, and after the round brackets: if learned is at least one.

28
00:02:17,009 --> 00:02:20,487
A crew that knows nothing gets two answers.

29
00:02:20,937 --> 00:02:24,415
A crew that logged the names gets three.

30
00:02:24,865 --> 00:02:27,909
The answer leads to a new scene.

31
00:02:28,359 --> 00:02:35,315
One take: Dace did not come out, and there is a cairn in a side room.

32
00:02:35,765 --> 00:02:44,026
One answer, and it leads on to The Rest of It, so this crew still hears the main recording.

33
00:02:45,226 --> 00:02:50,009
He said a side room, so there has to be one.

34
00:02:50,459 --> 00:02:54,807
A chamber, six hundred, with a passage to the Nave.

35
00:02:55,257 --> 00:02:56,996
That is Lecture 2.

36
00:02:57,446 --> 00:03:03,533
And a place in the middle of it, with a cone standing on it.

37
00:03:03,983 --> 00:03:05,722
That is Lecture 3.

38
00:03:06,172 --> 00:03:09,215
Now the answer shows it: reveal cairn.

39
00:03:09,665 --> 00:03:11,839
The key of the place.

40
00:03:12,289 --> 00:03:18,376
Not crypt: a room is not a place, and lint will not tell you.

41
00:03:19,576 --> 00:03:26,533
A side story is a quest that is not part of the main story. Three hashes.

42
00:03:26,983 --> 00:03:32,635
It starts when revealed, so it is asleep and out of the list.

43
00:03:33,085 --> 00:03:38,737
It is done when a ship is within four hundred of the cairn.

44
00:03:39,187 --> 00:03:43,100
And the answer starts it: a comma, accepts stayed.

45
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:45,724
Two things after one semicolon.

46
00:03:46,174 --> 00:03:54,870
Now, if you open Storm's Beacon you will find a section called Side Stories, and those are a different animal.

47
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,363
Each one says For, and a job.

48
00:03:58,813 --> 00:04:05,770
They belong to one person, and they are handed over when that person leaves the ship.

49
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,828
We get there in Lecture 8.

50
00:04:09,278 --> 00:04:17,104
Do not type that section today: lint will tell you nothing hands it out, and lint is right.

51
00:04:18,304 --> 00:04:21,348
A cutscene is a list of shots.

52
00:04:21,798 --> 00:04:26,146
A new section, and its key has to be cutscenes.

53
00:04:26,596 --> 00:04:33,117
The first record is the cutscene: its key, and Letterbox: yes for the black bars.

54
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:36,176
Then one record for each shot.

55
00:04:36,626 --> 00:04:38,800
Which cutscene it belongs to.

56
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:45,337
What the camera looks at: a role, the same word I write after reach.

57
00:04:45,787 --> 00:04:48,396
How near: close, medium or wide.

58
00:04:48,846 --> 00:04:53,628
Two words with a comma is a move: wide, then close.

59
00:04:54,078 --> 00:04:55,383
How many seconds.

60
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:58,876
And Overlay, lower_third: words at the bottom.

61
00:04:59,326 --> 00:05:02,804
A name, and under the fence, the line.

62
00:05:03,254 --> 00:05:08,037
Everywhere else in this file that line is my own note.

63
00:05:08,487 --> 00:05:15,009
Here the crew reads it: the name in blue, the line in white. Two rules.

64
00:05:15,459 --> 00:05:18,937
Keep it short: the crew cannot skip it.

65
00:05:19,387 --> 00:05:21,561
And keep each line short.

66
00:05:22,761 --> 00:05:23,761
Lint first.

67
00:05:24,211 --> 00:05:28,124
Nothing in this mission reads a section keyed cutscenes.

68
00:05:28,574 --> 00:05:36,400
It is right, and the end of its sentence is the fix: add the line that reads it.

69
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:39,893
That is a card, in two parts.

70
00:05:40,343 --> 00:05:47,735
Part one, in the map block, under the line that builds the ruin: read the Cutscenes section.

71
00:05:48,185 --> 00:05:51,663
I do not change a letter. Lint: clean.

72
00:05:52,113 --> 00:05:56,026
It is read now, and still nothing plays it.

73
00:05:56,476 --> 00:06:01,693
So the quest has to say when: Then: signal cairn_found. My word.

74
00:06:02,143 --> 00:06:06,491
Lint again: the word is sent and nothing hears it.

75
00:06:06,941 --> 00:06:18,246
Part two, at the very end of the script file: when the word cairn_found is sent, play the cutscene with this key, on every main screen.

76
00:06:18,696 --> 00:06:23,913
Two things here are mine: the word, and the key. Lint. Clean.

77
00:06:25,113 --> 00:06:26,113
Lint.

78
00:06:26,563 --> 00:06:29,607
I ask for the word by name.

79
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:32,665
It tells me learned only counts.

80
00:06:33,115 --> 00:06:36,593
Good: that answer would never have been offered.

81
00:06:37,043 --> 00:06:38,348
Put it back.

82
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:41,407
Now I misspell a subject. Clean.

83
00:06:41,857 --> 00:06:47,509
Lint reads the outside of a cutscene, not the inside of a shot.

84
00:06:47,959 --> 00:06:50,567
That shot would be left out.

85
00:06:51,017 --> 00:06:58,409
The game does say so, in one line, in the runtime log, after you have played it.

86
00:06:58,859 --> 00:07:00,163
Put it back.

87
00:07:00,613 --> 00:07:02,787
Now I misspell the overlay.

88
00:07:03,237 --> 00:07:09,324
Clean again, and this time nothing says anything: the shot plays with no words.

89
00:07:09,774 --> 00:07:15,861
There is a table on the page of the ones nothing tells you about.

90
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:18,485
Read it before you play.

91
00:07:19,685 --> 00:07:20,989
Through the ring.

92
00:07:21,439 --> 00:07:23,178
Rook, at the ring.

93
00:07:23,628 --> 00:07:24,933
Log the names.

94
00:07:25,383 --> 00:07:27,991
Across the Nave, up the tunnel.

95
00:07:28,441 --> 00:07:32,789
Rook, at the altar, and there is my third answer.

96
00:07:33,239 --> 00:07:34,978
The entry for Dace.

97
00:07:35,428 --> 00:07:37,167
Mark the side room.

98
00:07:37,617 --> 00:07:41,096
And the rest of it: mark the Gallery.

99
00:07:41,546 --> 00:07:48,937
A new contact on the far side of the Nave, and a new quest in the list.

100
00:07:49,387 --> 00:07:52,865
Back down, straight across, into the side room.

101
00:07:53,315 --> 00:07:55,489
And there it goes. Bars.

102
00:07:55,939 --> 00:08:00,287
The altar: the tally on the rim stops at forty-one.

103
00:08:00,737 --> 00:08:05,085
The cairn: forty-one stones, one for each day. And back.

104
00:08:05,535 --> 00:08:12,057
One thing you will notice: that panel in the corner says The Altar, Energy zero.

105
00:08:12,507 --> 00:08:17,724
It is the ship's own panel reading whatever the camera is on.

106
00:08:18,174 --> 00:08:23,391
It is not in my file, and I cannot take it away.

107
00:08:24,591 --> 00:08:29,809
Give Rook a line that only a crew who knows will hear.

108
00:08:30,259 --> 00:08:32,433
Pay for the side story.

109
00:08:32,883 --> 00:08:34,622
Add a third shot.

110
00:08:35,072 --> 00:08:41,159
Then break one line where lint can see it and one where it cannot.

111
00:08:41,609 --> 00:08:43,783
Next time, the main story.
